From 7d8762abe5a840d0cf06f0c41bb23dd7818ff475 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 07:08:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 221/258] test(cpu): harden AVX2 layout boundary evidence

External review follow-ups:
- replace the sampled descriptor byte-mutation test with an exhaustive
  len(wire)-position sweep: reserved header bytes 20-23 are explicitly
  asserted benign (byte-identical output), every other position must be
  rejected and leave the caller buffer untouched;
- add a cross-backend regression that pins the PXLD-v2 wire bytes and the
  LayoutPlan digest to AVX-512 for every native layout op kind and dtype;
- allow a per-case sha256 manifest (PYPTO_X_AVX2_LAYOUT_SHA256_MANIFEST)
  so external reviewers can re-verify every bitwise comparison.
